<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148" title="View the profile of Lhyra">Lhyra</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 8<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9708#msg9708"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9708#msg9708">Re: LDON drama 4 j00</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #15 on:</b> August 03, 2004, 03:08:26 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Oh..btw<br /><br />The paladin was asking for a &quot;symbol&quot;.  What he really meant...was peridot.  He was asking the whole time for a peridot to cast his &quot;virtue&quot;.  Sheeesh.  You guys don&#039;t know how to read noob.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><img src="http://hometown.aol.com/ktenderheart/AK/images/ruthann2.jpg" alt="" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg9710"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=707" title="View the profile of Corolinth">Corolinth</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 42<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/gohper.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=707"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9710#msg9710"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9710#msg9710">Re: LDON drama 4 j00</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #16 on:</b> August 03, 2004, 04:11:12 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9702#msg9702">Quote from: Iniquitous on August 03, 2004, 02:37:54 pm</a></div><div class="quote">I heard about this advent, but had not seen a log until this thread.<br /><br />Here are all the facts I really need:<br /><br />1. You zoned in without permission.</div><br />Right here, I&#039;d have assumed he was the only person in the group that had even half a brain.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">2. You were mouthy.</div><br />No moreso than any competent player would be when surrounded by dumbasses.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">The wizard wasn&#039;t asking for Virtue he was asking the Paladin if he had the 1100 pt pally buff that he must have been comparing to virtue: Guidance.&nbsp; He even refers to it as the &quot;pally virt spell&quot;.&nbsp; He questions the request for symbol because the -pally- is asking for a symbol when the only person in the group that can cast symbols is the pally.&nbsp; The pally was definitely a newb.&nbsp; Silverblades, and everybody else involved most likely, was expecting a bard to keep all mobs mezzed that weren&#039;t on main tank.&nbsp; You knew at this point that you had a newb tank, and with only a dru healing, I don&#039;t know why you expected anything but single mob fights.</div><br />Time to give a ranger&#039;s perspective. As a ranger I don&#039;t trust anybody else in a normal ldon to be able to tie their shoelaces, let alone do their job. This means that I&#039;m expecting to have to root every single pull, because the complicated process of targetting mobs and mezzing them is completely beyond the limited scope of our enchanter or bard. If a ranger is in a normal ldon adventure and he&#039;s expecting the bard to be able to mez, then he&#039;s a moron. The one time you get lazy and let your guard down in a normal ldon is the time you end up with 5 drooling feebs.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">From what Silverblades had to say the wizard basically soloed most of the advent root nuking and they still won with plenty of time.</div><br />Good for them. They could&#039;ve actually had a decent finish time if they&#039;d paid attention and done their job rather than booting the bard.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">What I find most disturbing about your post is that you think it&#039;s OK to zone in without the group&#039;s permission.&nbsp; That&#039;s pretty irresponsible and definitely not something a mature EQ player should be doing.&nbsp; If you&#039;re not leading the encounter, you stay put until told otherwise.</div><br />It is. Some people are complete newbs, and need you to hold their hand. Still others don&#039;t realize that they&#039;re complete newbs, and get in the way.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">That must suck that you got a failure message, since they won the LDON with 30 minutes to spare.</div><br />Winning with 30 minutes to spare means it took them an hour. An hour is an acceptable win time... in a hard ldon.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />&lt;Echoes in Eternity&gt;
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg9711"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=748" title="View the profile of Iniquitous">Iniquitous</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 12<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=748"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9711#msg9711"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9711#msg9711">Re: LDON drama 4 j00</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #17 on:</b> August 03, 2004, 04:20:37 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I think you&#039;re exactly right.&nbsp; I think the wizard was trying to prevent the multi pulls from taking out the newb pally and the under-powered druid.<br /><br />The ranger has anger management issues.&nbsp; I&#039;ll give you that.&nbsp; He&#039;s not a bad player, but he&#039;s been yelled at so many times for trying to CC adds when other people were handling it that he probably was hesitant.&nbsp; He&#039;s not super-experienced, but he&#039;s definitely not a newb like the pally.<br /><br />However, and in response to a previous post as well, I believe if you intentionally run straight into an advent while everyone else is still buffing, you&#039;re immediately reducing your in-group reputation by 50%.&nbsp; I know a lot of people would be offended, and you ran into 5 people that feel the same way.&nbsp; It&#039;s not about the real impact of the action.&nbsp; Yeah, you can probably win, regardless of zoning in early, but you&#039;re making a decision for the group without even asking.&nbsp; The response to your pulls has to take into account you zoning in early.&nbsp; If you had not zoned in early, I doubt this disagreement would have ever happened.&nbsp; I think you&#039;re verbal remarks would still have irritated some people, but they probably wouldn&#039;t have ever said anything about it.&nbsp; Well, the ranger might have, but I&#039;ve noted his anger issues above.<br /><br />-Iniquitous
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg9714"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=748" title="View the profile of Iniquitous">Iniquitous</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 12<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=748"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9714#msg9714"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=980.msg9714#msg9714">Re: LDON drama 4 j00</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #18 on:</b> August 03, 2004, 04:31:47 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">No moreso than any competent player would be when surrounded by dumbasses.</div><br />There&#039;s no reason to be mouthy.&nbsp; I expect competent players to be able to deal without mouthing off.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">It is. Some people are complete newbs, and need you to hold their hand. Still others don&#039;t realize that they&#039;re complete newbs, and get in the way.<br /></div>Unless you can solo the ldon and win, it&#039;s certainly not acceptable.&nbsp; Regardless of the bard&#039;s skill level, I doubt he could solo the entire advent successfully.&nbsp; Add to that it&#039;s simply impolite, which is enough to make it wrong all by itself, in my book.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Winning with 30 minutes to spare means it took them an hour. An hour is an acceptable win time... in a hard ldon.<br /></div>Any win is acceptable when adversity is involved.&nbsp; A newb pally, combined with a weak healer, added to a lost bard equals adversity.<br /><br />How good it must feel to insult a group of challenged (some mentally, some otherwise) players for pulling out a win.&nbsp; Does it make you feel better?&nbsp; I&#039;m just curious.&nbsp; I often wonder why people bother posting responses like that.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
